# .kbignore — paths excluded from knowledge-base analysis (/kb:init, /kb:update, /kb:check).
#
# Syntax is the same as .gitignore: globs, `#` comments, `!` negation, trailing `/` for dirs.
# Built-in defaults are ALWAYS applied, even if this file is empty. This file only adds to them.
#
# --- Built-in defaults (already in effect; listed for reference only) ---
# node_modules/  .git/  vendor/  dist/  build/  out/  target/  obj/  coverage/
# .next/  .cache/  .turbo/  .venv/  venv/  __pycache__/  .idea/  .vscode/
# *.lock  package-lock.json  yarn.lock  pnpm-lock.yaml  *.min.js  *.min.css  *.map
# *.generated.*  *.png  *.jpg  *.svg  *.woff*  *.ttf  *.mp4  *.pdf  *.zip

# --- From .gitignore ---
docs/superpowers/
.worktrees/

# --- Directories worth considering ---
# test/
test/fixtures/
# docs/
.agentics/
# .claude/

# --- Common test file patterns ---
# *.test.*
# *.spec.*
# *.snap
